title: 'Fix `paras_inherent::enter_backed_candidate_code_upgrade` benchmark for small block lengths'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The `enter_backed_candidate_code_upgrade` benchmark built a candidate carrying a code upgrade
    of `max_code_size` bytes. The paras inherent caps its proof size at the maximum block length
    and the proof size of a backed candidate is its encoded size, so such a candidate does not fit
    into the block on runtimes whose block length leaves no room for the rest of the candidate,
    for example when `max_code_size` equals `MAX_CODE_SIZE` (5 MiB) and the block length is 5 MiB
    as well. The candidate was then dropped by `apply_weight_limit` and the benchmark failed with
    `InherentDataFilteredDuringExecution`.

    The benchmark now caps the code upgrade at the largest one that can actually be included in a
    block and asserts that the candidate fits, so the failure mode is a clear assertion instead of
    a filtered inherent.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
